{
  "name": "AppEvent",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "event": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "What happened, as a short machine name: session_start, session_end, page_view, task_created, task_create_failed, task_completed, calendar_sync, calendar_sync_failed, app_error, duplicate_detected, alarm_choice (every choice made on an alarm or a reminder's notification, as the phone reports it to cancelTaskNotifications; props: task_id, choice snooze | dismiss | ignored | closed | later, at, how, minutes, report_id, task_gone; the owner health check counts missed alarms from these), reminder_sent (a push that went out, kept from the send ledger when sendLedger.ledgerPrune clears it after 3 days, so reminder history outlives the ledger; props: task_id, kind, source, send_at = when it went out, and from Nov 11 2026 outcome ('sent' = OneSignal says it reached a phone, 'unknown' = OneSignal couldn't say) and id (the OneSignal id); created_date is when it was kept; Anna, Nov 1 2026. Rows kept before Nov 11 2026 have no outcome and were NOT checked with OneSignal: some are bookings that were cancelled before they went, or pushes that reached no phone, so check with OneSignal (debugNotifications mode sent_to) before saying someone got one), reminder_unreached (from Nov 11 2026: a push OneSignal tried and that reached no phone, because the app was uninstalled or its push sign-up was dead; the person never saw it; same props, outcome 'nobody'), reminder_cancelled (a row first kept as reminder_sent that OneSignal shows was cancelled before it went; renamed by hand when found). A booking cancelled before it went is otherwise not kept at all."
    },
    "user_email": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Who the event belongs to. Set by whoever writes the event so records stay groupable per user without reading any personal content."
    },
    "session_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Random id generated once per app open (lives in sessionStorage). Lets session length and the sequence of actions inside one visit be reconstructed without any device identifier."
    },
    "seconds": {
      "type": "number",
      "description": "Duration in seconds, for events that measure time: how long a session stayed open, or how long a task existed before being completed."
    },
    "page": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Route the event happened on (e.g. /Home). Path only \u2014 never query strings, which can carry content."
    },
    "props": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Small bag of non-identifying detail for this event only \u2014 counts, flags, error messages, timings. Never task titles, diary text, names, addresses or anything the user wrote."
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "event"
  ],
  "rls": {
    "read": false,
    "create": {},
    "update": false,
    "delete": false
  }
}